--- Blocks or releases one curated input action for the calling resource.
---
--- Requires `input.actions`. The vocabulary is curated rather than an engine enum dump, because Cyberpunk has no single input-blocking lever: five unrelated mechanisms serve five families of action and a large minority of actions cannot be refused at all. Blockable today: `Movement`, `Map`, `Hub`, `FastTravel`, `Attack`. An action outside the vocabulary is refused with `unknown_action`; one this engine cannot refuse with `action_not_blockable`; one Open77 already blocks unconditionally (`PhotoMode`, `Scanner`, `Quickhack`, `CallVehicle`, `Journal`) with `action_already_enforced`. Nothing is accepted and silently ignored. Claims are owned by the calling resource: two resources may block the same action, `blocked=false` removes only the caller's claim, and everything a resource holds is released when it stops. See `wiki/input-blocking.md` and `docs/research/input-action-blocking.md`.
---
--- Permissions: input.actions
--- Since: 2.31.13+op77.67
---@param action any
---@param blocked boolean
---@return any true true, otherwise false
---@return any reason reason: permission_denied:input.actions, invalid_action_arguments, unknown_action, action_not_blockable, action_already_enforced, action_blocking_unavailable_on_this_host
function Open77.input.setActionBlocked(action, blocked) end

